  "activity": {
    "id": "activity_dna_structure_replication",
    "name": "DNA Double Helix Structure and Semiconservative Replication",
    "description": "A ten-concept AR lab guiding students from the schematic ladder representation of DNA through the realistic double helix, antiparallel 5'-to-3' directionality, complementary base pairing, the enzymatic machinery of the replication fork (helicase, SSBs, DNA polymerase, DNA ligase), leading vs lagging strand synthesis, and the semiconservative nature of replication, closing with a recap of all concept areas.",
    "workplace": "wp_dna_structure_replication",
    "start": "step1_schematic_ladder",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step1_schematic_ladder",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "The Schematic DNA Ladder",
          "description": "Observe the flat ladder representation of DNA. Two vertical lines represent the sugar-phosphate backbones; horizontal rungs represent base pairs, color-coded by identity (A=red, T=blue, G=yellow, C=green). Note how each rung is built from two labeled bases meeting in the middle."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_ladder_schematic",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_intro_structure",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step1"
          },
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "marker_helix_model",
            "duration": 2000
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step2_helix_geometry",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "From Ladder to Helix",
          "description": "Watch the flat ladder twist into the realistic double-helix shape. The backbones spiral around a common axis while base pairs stack along the interior. The helix completes one turn approximately every ten base pairs. Toggle between schematic and realistic views to build the mental mapping."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_ladder_to_helix",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_helix_twist",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step2"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step3_antiparallel_directionality",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Antiparallel Strands and 5' / 3' Directionality",
          "description": "Directional arrows appear along each backbone: one strand points up, the other down. Labels mark the 5' and 3' termini of each strand. The two strands always run in opposite directions \u2014 an arrangement forced by the directional chemistry of the sugar-phosphate backbone. Rotate the helix to confirm the arrows from any angle."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_helix_arrows",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_5prime",
              "poi": "poi_5prime_end",
              "text": "5' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_3prime",
              "poi": "poi_3prime_end",
              "text": "3' end"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_antiparallel",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_helix",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step3"
          },
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "marker_basepair_station",
            "duration": 2000
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step4_basepairing_activity",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Complementary Base-Pairing Activity",
          "description": "A partial ladder shows a complete labeled strand (5'-ATGCCAGT-3') on the left and an empty backbone on the right. Drag bases from the palette below to complete the complementary strand. Correct pairs (A-T, G-C) snap into place and display hydrogen bonds: two dashed lines for A-T, three for G-C. Incorrect pairings are rejected."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_base_palette",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_video_basepairing_demo",
              "poi": "default"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_hydrogen_bonds_at",
              "poi": "poi_rung_top",
              "text": "A-T: 2 hydrogen bonds"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_hydrogen_bonds_gc",
              "poi": "poi_rung_bottom",
              "text": "G-C: 3 hydrogen bonds"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_base_palette",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_basepairing",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_base_palette",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_dna_ladder",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            }
          ]
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step4"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step5_helicase_unwinding",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Helicase Unwinds the Double Helix",
          "description": "Helicase, labeled and positioned at one end of the helix, moves along the DNA and unwinds the two strands, breaking hydrogen bonds and exposing the bases. Watch helicase work its way along a stretch of DNA, opening the helix so the strands can serve as templates."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_helicase_unwind",
              "poi": "poi_fork_front"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_helicase",
              "poi": "poi_fork_front",
              "text": "Helicase"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_helicase",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step5"
          },
          {
            "mode": "detect",
            "id": "marker_fork_zone",
            "duration": 2000
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step6_ssb_stabilization",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Single-Strand Binding Proteins Stabilize the Strands",
          "description": "As helicase separates the two strands, single-strand binding proteins (SSBs), rendered as small labeled spheres, attach to each exposed strand. SSBs prevent the unstable single strands from re-pairing or folding back on themselves, keeping them accessible for replication."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_ssb_attach",
              "poi": "poi_leading_strand"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_ssb_attach",
              "poi": "poi_lagging_strand"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_ssb",
              "poi": "poi_leading_strand",
              "text": "SSB proteins"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_ssb",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "next_step6"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step7_leading_strand",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "DNA Polymerase and the Leading Strand",
          "description": "DNA polymerase appears on the template strand oriented so synthesis proceeds in the same direction as the moving fork. Because polymerase can only extend a strand 5' to 3', it travels 3' to 5' along this template, continuously synthesizing the leading strand as free nucleotides pair and are added. Note that polymerase requires a primer to begin."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_anim_leading_synthesis",
              "poi": "poi_leading_strand"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_polymerase_leading",
              "poi": "poi_leading_strand",
              "text": "DNA Polymerase (Leading Strand)"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_replication_fork",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_leading",
              "poi": "default"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": []
        },
        "exit": {
